10
00:00:30,845 --> 00:00:32,536
Both halves matter equally.

11
00:00:33,086 --> 00:00:37,719
Five lectures, and notice the shape: one on what these tools can and can't do

12
00:00:37,719 --> 00:00:42,773
honestly, one on the actual batch, and three on the specific ways a batch goes wrong

13
00:00:42,773 --> 00:00:43,977
and how to catch it.

14
00:00:43,977 --> 00:00:45,601
That balance is deliberate.

15
00:00:45,601 --> 00:00:50,415
A course that only shows the wins teaches you to trust a generator more than you

16
00:00:50,415 --> 00:00:50,836
